  "term": "Silenor",
  "definition": "Silenor is doxepin, a tricyclic antidepressant that can reduce depression, anxiety, and itching. It works by increasing the availability of norepinephrine and serotonin in the brain and also blocks several receptors, including histamine receptors, which helps explain its antipruritic effects.",
